## Summary

**Root cause** — `TagsHelper.removeTag()` (`omniNotes/src/main/java/it/feio/android/omninotes/utils/TagsHelper.java`):

```java
title   = title.replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), "");
content = content.replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), "");
```

`String.replaceAll` performs an **unanchored regex substring** replacement. So when a tag is unchecked in the "select tags" dialog (`DetailFragment.tagNote()` / `ListFragment.tagNote()`), removing `#test` also stripped the matching prefix out of every other tag sharing that header — `#testa` → `a`, `#testb` → `b` — exactly as reported. Passing the tag as a raw regex was a second latent defect: a tag containing regex metacharacters (e.g. `#c++`, `#a(b)`) would either be misinterpreted or throw `PatternSyntaxException`.

**Fix** — remove only whole tokens, and treat the tag as a literal:

```java
private static String removeTagFromText(String text, Tag tagToRemove) {
    if (text == null || tagToRemove == null || tagToRemove.getText() == null) {
        return text;
    }
    // (?<!\S) and (?!\S) ensure that the tag is surrounded by whitespaces or text boundaries
    return text.replaceAll("(?<!\\S)" + Pattern.quote(tagToRemove.getText()) + "(?!\\S)", "");
}
```

The zero-width `(?<!\S)` / `(?!\S)` guards require the match to be delimited by whitespace or a string boundary, which mirrors how `retrieveTags()` tokenizes tags (whitespace-separated, `^#[^\p{Z}]+`). `Pattern.quote` makes the tag literal. Existing behavior for legitimate removals (multiple occurrences, tags at line start/end, title and content) is unchanged.

**Verification**
- `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` → BUILD SUCCESSFUL.
- Added regression test `removesOnlyExactlyMatchingTagsFromNote` asserting that removing `#test` from `"... #test #testa #testb #test"` drops `#test` while preserving `#testa` and `#testb`; the full `TagsHelperTest` suite passes (5 tests, 0 failures). This test fails against the original code.

